# Print link

Use a button when the action opens the browser print dialog, and a link only when a separate printable page exists. Opening the dialog does not mean anything was printed, so never say it did.

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation. They do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Printing helps with offline recovery notes, maintenance notes and a household quick reference, for example a “Restore from a backup” checklist. Include the page title, revision and meaningful text in the print output. A printed chart also needs its unit, selected period and a data alternative.

## Structure and behaviour

Hide action controls and decorative navigation in print styles, and keep warnings and content. For a multi-part guide, build a complete print view before offering a link to it.

## Home Assistant boundary

Both examples call window.print() only when the person selects Print this example. That opens the browser print dialog for the isolated example document. The action controls are left out of the printout and the content stays. No PDF is generated or uploaded. Without JavaScript, use the browser’s own Print command. The example button stays disabled. Test the real print preview, including expanded and collapsed history.

